  "articleBody": "Thinking about adding some built-in shelving to your home? That's a fantastic way to add storage and character! But before you jump in, let's talk about a few things. First, really think about what you'll store. Will it be books, decor, or heavy items? This helps determine the design and load capacity needed. You'll also want to consider if the design fits the room's existing look and trim. It’s important to make sure it flows seamlessly with your home. Don't forget about existing wall features like outlets – sometimes they need to be moved, and that can get a bit tricky. Finally, decide if you want fixed or adjustable shelves. Fixed shelves can look super clean, but adjustable ones offer more flexibility down the road. If your vision involves moving utilities or significant wall changes, it might be a good idea to chat with a pro like HH Remodeling LLC here in Aurora. We can help you navigate those bigger considerations to make sure your shelves are perfect and functional.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}